---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import DocShell from "../../components/DocShell.astro";
import CommandBlock from "../../components/CommandBlock.astro";
---

<Layout title="CLI Reference | ArkheionX Docs" description="ArkheionX public command reference and execution boundaries.">
  <DocShell>
    <p class="page-kicker">Use</p>
    <h1>CLI reference.</h1>
    <p class="doc-deck">Public commands in the v3.9.0 source state. Use <code>arkheionx COMMAND --help</code> for complete flags.</p>

    <h2>Environment and demos</h2>
    <div class="definition-grid">
      <div><dt><code>version</code></dt><dd>Print package and milestone metadata.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>doctor [repo]</code></dt><dd>Check install health, project layout, and Foundry availability without building.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>demo</code></dt><dd>List, inspect, or copy bundled local demo fixtures.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>validate-config</code></dt><dd>Validate an ArkheionX JSON configuration.</dd></div>
    </div>

    <h2>Orientation</h2>
    <div class="definition-grid">
      <div><dt><code>scan ROOT</code></dt><dd>Run the local readiness and value-flow scan.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>open [repo]</code></dt><dd>Compact project orientation.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>map [repo]</code></dt><dd>Render protocol roles, journeys, flow, and review targets.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>flow [repo]</code></dt><dd>Focus on candidate money-flow edges and Mermaid output.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>hunt [repo]</code></dt><dd>Rank surfaces for manual investigation.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>search QUERY</code></dt><dd>Search bundled local security-memory metadata.</dd></div>
    </div>

    <h2>Review map</h2>
    <div class="definition-grid">
      <div><dt><code>review-map [repo]</code></dt><dd>Build the combined roles, paths, assumptions, gaps, proof suggestions, and evidence-link surface.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>value-paths [repo]</code></dt><dd>Render focused candidate value paths.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>assumptions [repo]</code></dt><dd>Render focused inferred assumptions.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>test-gap-map [repo]</code></dt><dd>Render focused local test gaps.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>proof-plan [repo]</code></dt><dd>Generate target-specific local proof suggestions.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>evidence-links [repo]</code></dt><dd>Cross-reference review targets and existing local artifacts.</dd></div>
    </div>

    <h2>Evidence and packaging</h2>
    <div class="definition-grid">
      <div><dt><code>prove [repo]</code></dt><dd>Generate a local Foundry proof scaffold. <code>--run</code> explicitly enables targeted test execution.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>trace [repo]</code></dt><dd>Summarize proof or trace state. <code>--run</code> explicitly enables targeted execution.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>evidence [repo]</code></dt><dd>Build a compact local evidence package from existing artifacts.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>report [repo]</code></dt><dd>Create a responsible local report draft from evidence.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>evidence-status [repo]</code></dt><dd>Inspect artifact state by target.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>validate-artifacts [repo]</code></dt><dd>Validate generated proof, evidence, and report artifacts.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>local-validate REPO</code></dt><dd>Parse saved Foundry output; this command records provenance and does not run Foundry.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>review-package [repo]</code></dt><dd>Collect existing artifacts into a manifest-backed local package.</dd></div>
    </div>

    <h2>Output control</h2>
    <CommandBlock command={`arkheionx review-map . --json --no-write
arkheionx value-paths . --top 5
arkheionx review-package . --strict --export zip`} />
    <p>Common focused commands support JSON output, no-write operation, target filtering, and explicit output paths. Check command help before scripting.</p>

    <div class="doc-note"><strong>Execution boundary:</strong> options named <code>--run</code> and <code>--build</code> can invoke local Foundry operations. They are not enabled by default.</div>
  </DocShell>
</Layout>
